Container.Requires:
BEFORE CLICKING APPLY: Prusa Connect runs as UID/GID 10001:10001. Unraid-created appdata directories may not be writable by this user. In Unraid Terminal, if you kept the default host paths, run:

APPDATA="/mnt/user/appdata/prusa-connect"
mkdir -p "$APPDATA"/{config.d,data,storage,files,tmp}
chown -R 10001:10001 "$APPDATA"/{config.d,data,storage,files,tmp}
ls -ldn "$APPDATA"/{config.d,data,storage,files,tmp}

If you changed any host paths in the installer, substitute those exact paths. Do not chown your entire appdata share or directories used by other containers. If already restarting with "permission denied", stop this container, fix ownership, then start it. FULL STEP-BY-STEP GUIDE: https://github.com/bleugray/prusa-connect-unraid#installation-step-by-step

FIRST START: Open container Logs, find setup_code=XXXX-XXXX-XXXX, and enter it into the browser wizard. Choose Local Accounts with an administrator for a real installation; selecting no sign-in makes adding users afterward difficult. Choose /storage for local files and restart after setup. Keep the setup code private.

PORT: The default WebUI/API container port is 8080. If occupied on Unraid, change only the Host Port. The base /config/config.yaml file is optional; the wizard works without it.
